{title: Let Your Face Shine}
{subtitle: Psalms 80:4}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 126}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] |
| [Bb7] | ×8
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Gm7] | [Gm7] |
| [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Shepherd [Eb]of Israel listen to us [Gm7]now
You who lead [Abmaj7]Joseph like a flock
Enthroned upon the cherubim
Shine forth with your [Eb]holy might
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Before Ep[Gm7]hraim and Benjamin
Manasseh [Abmaj7]stands in the light
Stir up your power and come
Save us from this [Eb]heavy night
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Restore us O God
Let your face shine [Gm7]on us
That we may be [Abmaj7]saved
In your grace and trust
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]God of hosts how long
[Gm7]Will your anger smolder on
[Abmaj7]Against the prayer of your people
Let the tears be gone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Restore us O [Eb]God
Let your face shine [Gm7]on us
That we may be [Abmaj7]saved
In your grace and trust
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Fm7]Fed with bread of tears
[Gm7]Drinking sorrow by the measure
[Abmaj7]Causing strife to neighbors
Enemies laughing together
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Abmaj7] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Gm7] |
| [Gm7] | [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Let your face shine [Eb][Gm7]
Let your face shine
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] |
| [Eb] | [Eb] |
